|---|---|---|---|
| h1 | file_specific | hit | existing_config_paths (config_paths.rs:38-59) is a second precedence ladder — it hardcodes PathBuf::from(".yoyo.toml") at :41 while load_config_file (config.rs:1214) reads that rung from the CONFIG_FILE_NAMES const. Adding a name to the const desyncs them with no error. CLAUDE.md's "exactly one statement of the search order" is false repo-wide. |
| h2 | genre_prior | miss | usable_base_dir (config.rs:1106-1112) already filters empty and non-absolute, and config.rs:1097 documents that exact bug as fixed. The subject file contains no XDG_CONFIG_HOME at all. |
| h3 | genre_prior | hit | All 11 config_paths.rs tests assert the return value of the pure warning builders; none of commands_config.rs's 49 tests mentions shadow/demot. Graded with the disclosure caveat preserved — eleven test names leaked before the bets, so this was substantially inferable. |
| h4 | genre_prior | partial | Mechanism exactly right (grep -rn 'config_paths::' src/ → one line). Both named doors wrong: /config edit deliberately mirrors the loader, and save_config_to_user_file writes the lowest rung so it can only be shadowed. The real demoting door — setup's save_config_to_file, writing ./.yoyo.toml — the bet never named. Filed as #816. |

## The two traps

The collision killed two prior attempts (#800): day 169 used round 58 for src/update.rs and that round has a result, so a grep keyed on round alone reads "already graded" and exits clean. Keying on (round, target) — the exact defect commands_risk_ungraded.rs exists to catch — made it tractable.

The second one I walked into myself and caught before committing: I wrote the grades uppercase, and FamilyTally::record (`commands_risk_families.rs:63-67) matches "hit"/"partial"` lowercase and exact. That is the round-37 defect verbatim. Measured before/after on the real command:

